      "body": "## Motivation\n\nSM100 swap-AB decode attention for DeepSeek-V4.1 admits at most 8 query rows. DSpark verify sends 5 rows per request (block size 5), so only batch size 1 takes swap-AB; batch size 2 and up fall back to FlashMLA. FlashMLA pads q to 64 heads and runs split-KV, so its time is flat at about 24 µs across 5–40 rows, while swap-AB is 2.7x faster at 5 rows and grows with the row count.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `decode_attention_sm100.py`: admit up to 40 rows (`MAX_ROWS`) on SM100, so TP4 verify up to batch size 8 takes swap-AB. The kernel grid is (rows, KV tiles) and no program depends on the row count, so the cap is only a dispatch choice. The gfx950 path keeps its 8-row `MAX_BATCH`.\n- `test_swapab_attention.py`: add 20- and 40-row cases and a 40-row CUDA graph replay; the per-row lengths now repeat so they cover any batch.\n\n## Kernel timing\n\nGB300, 16 heads (TP4), one decode layer shape (SWA 128 + extra KV 512), CUDA graph timing, µs per call:\n\n| rows | batch size (verify) | swap-AB | FlashMLA | ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 5 | 1 | 8.8 | 23.7 | 0.37 |\n| 10 | 2 | 9.3 | 23.9 | 0.39 |\n| 20 | 4 | 12.5 | 23.9 | 0.52 |\n| 24 | — | 13.1 | 23.8 | 0.55 |\n| 40 | 8 | 20.1 | 24.2 | 0.83 |\n\nBreak-even is near 48 rows; 40 leaves a margin.\n\n## Benchmark\n\nAgentX, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash FP4 on GB300, TP4/EP1, one hour per run, DSpark with simulated acceptance length 3.51. Both arms use `lmsysorg/sglang:nightly-dev-cu13-20261012-e6072935`; \"this PR\" overlays the changed attention files onto the same image. Server flags: `--tensor-parallel-size 4 --expert-parallel-size 1 --mem-fraction-static 0.8 --chunked-prefill-size 16384 --cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 128 --max-running-requests 128 --swa-prefix-tails 4096 --tokenizer-worker-num 4`, with `--prefill-decode-interval` 0 at c8 and 192 at c16.\n\n| conc | main: P90 tok/s/user @ tok/s/GPU | this PR | P90 | median tok/s/user |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | 413.3 @ 16,089 | 411.3 @ 16,184 | −0.5% | 577 → 610 (+5.7%) |\n| 16 | 422.0 @ 28,885 | 442.4 @ 29,108 | +4.8% | 538 → 559 (+4.0%) |\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nGSM8K, all 1319 questions, 5-shot, real MTP verification (no simulated acceptance), 64 concurrent requests, TP4 on GB300:\n\n| main | this PR |\n|---|---|\n| 0.9696 | 0.9711 |\n\n## Unit tests\n\n`test/registered/kernels/ops/attention/dsv4/test_swapab_attention.py` passes on GB300.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38840939248](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38840939248)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38840938851](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38840938851)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38840938916](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38840938916)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
